      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you really want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I can enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
