       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day of metformin is about twice the maximum dose. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose this high. Nothing about this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) makes it safe. It could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals. I can enter either now.\n- **Help with the timing.** If you need glycemic control sorted out quickly, a faster option such as insulin might fit better. That's your call and the pharmacist's, and I can enter whatever you decide.\n- **Send it through pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this patient needs an exception, a direct conversation with pharmacy or the attending would be the right route. I can enter an order after that review, with a note documenting it.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
